{"by":"aryaman_darda","descendants":3,"id":50523377,"kids":[50556557,50526579,50544535,50525213],"score":78,"text":"I type &quot;forklift&quot; on a live warehouse camera, and tamserve finds and tracks both forklifts, including the one driving in. Then I add &quot;person&quot; without stopping it.<p>tamserve runs Meta&#x27;s SAM 3 on live camera feeds. SAM 3&#x27;s own tracker handles one recorded video at a time, runs at about 8 fps, and runs out of memory on long videos. tamserve uses SAM 3 to find objects every few frames and a lightweight tracker (EdgeTAM) to follow them in between, with one copy of each model shared across all your cameras.<p>*On one RTX 4090:*<p>* *Any object you name:* 4x faster than SAM 3&#x27;s tracker, at 92% of its accuracy\n* *People:* 16 cameras at once, 14x less GPU per frame, and slightly more accurate than SAM 3 (89.6 vs 87.8 HOTA)\n* *Memory:* flat at 3.5 GB on a 3,000 frame video, where SAM 3 runs out at frame 423<p>*Worth a look if you&#x27;re building:*<p>* Warehouse or factory safety (forklifts, pallets, hard hats)\n* Security or retail camera analytics\n* Home or elder care monitoring\n* Robotics, wildlife or lab monitoring\n* Annotation tools for long videos<p>`pip install &quot;tamserve[sam3]&quot;`<p>Please give me any and all feedback or edit tamserve to meet your needs, and a star helps if you find it useful!","time":1794863679,"title":"Show HN: Open-source, real-time object tracking for live video feeds","type":"story","url":"https://github.com/aryamandarda/tamserve"}
